From 5d57b3670f33748e163495229312e735828f2342 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Md Arif <111168803+sabamdarif@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 17:08:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drop soffice.sh LD_PRELOAD in favor of linking with -z global

The wrapper preloaded libsofficeapp.so, libvclplug_gtk3lo.so and
libsfxlo.so because LD_PRELOAD was the only mechanism Bionic honored
for putting a library's weak vague-linkage symbols (exception
type_info, dynamic_cast RTTI) ahead of later dlopen groups. That
approach was whack-a-mole: each preloaded library only unifies the
type_info copies it happens to export itself.

The package now links every library with -Wl,-z,global, baking
DF_1_GLOBAL into each .so. Bionic adds DF_1_GLOBAL libraries to the
global group at load time regardless of how they are loaded, so the
first-loaded copy of every type_info wins process-wide and typed
catches and dynamic_casts match across all components in all
directions. The preload list is redundant with that and is removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 desktop/scripts/soffice.sh | 47 +++++++-------------------------------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

diff --git a/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh b/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh
index bf5a5f6b1..567566dca 100755
--- a/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh
+++ b/desktop/scripts/soffice.sh
@@ -53,45 +53,14 @@ cd "$sd_dirname" || exit $?
 sd_prog=$(pwd)
 cd "$sd_cwd" || exit $?
 
-# Termux/Bionic: unlike glibc, Bionic's dynamic linker resolves weak
-# (vague-linkage) symbols per dlopen group, not process-wide. Every dlopen'd
-# UNO component therefore binds the C++ exception type_info objects
-# (_ZTIN3com3sun4star...) to its own local copy, and because libc++abi
-# matches catch clauses by type_info pointer identity, UNO exceptions thrown
-# in one .so escape every typed catch in another .so (observed as the
-# startup abort / white Start Center window).
-#
-# Preloading libsofficeapp.so force-sets DF_1_GLOBAL on it at load time,
-# which is the ONLY mechanism Bionic honors for placing a library's symbols
-# ahead of a later dlopen group's own copies: on-device tests show that both
-# dlopen(RTLD_GLOBAL) at load time and later RTLD_NOLOAD|RTLD_GLOBAL
-# "promotion" do NOT affect how subsequently loaded libraries bind these
-# symbols, but LD_PRELOAD does. With this, every component binds the
-# exception type_info base chain to libsofficeapp's copies and typed
-# catches match again.
-#
-# libvclplug_gtk3lo.so must be preloaded too: it is dlopen'd as a VCL
-# plugin (not DT_NEEDED anywhere), so it sits outside libsofficeapp's
-# startup closure and its weld::* / gtk widget classes get their own local
-# type_info copies. dynamic_cast also matches by type_info pointer
-# identity, so e.g. svt::ToolboxController::initialize's
-# dynamic_cast<weld::Toolbar*> on a GtkInstanceToolbar returns null and
-# the sidebar toolbar setup crashes on a null vcl::Window
-# (ImageOrientationController ctor) as soon as a document opens.
-#
-# libsfxlo.so must be preloaded as well: preloading only unifies the
-# exception types libsofficeapp itself happens to emit, and
-# css::container::NoSuchElementException is not among them (readelf shows
-# no _ZTIN3com3sun4star9container22NoSuchElementExceptionE in its dynsym).
-# configmgr (dlopen'd UNO component) throws NoSuchElementException for
-# missing config keys as normal control flow; sfx2::FileDialogHelper's
-# typed catch in libsfxlo compares against a different type_info copy and
-# misses, so the exception falls through to a generic handler and every
-# GUI save aborts with "General input/output error" before the file
-# dialog even opens. With libsfxlo preloaded its exported copy wins the
-# global lookup for both the throwing component and the catch site.
-LD_PRELOAD="$sd_prog/libsofficeapp.so:$sd_prog/libvclplug_gtk3lo.so:$sd_prog/libsfxlo.so${LD_PRELOAD:+:$LD_PRELOAD}"
-export LD_PRELOAD
+# Termux/Bionic: every LibreOffice library is linked with -Wl,-z,global
+# (DF_1_GLOBAL, see the package build.sh), which puts each library in the
+# dynamic linker's global group as it loads. That unifies the weak
+# vague-linkage symbols (exception type_info, RTTI used by dynamic_cast)
+# process-wide, which Bionic otherwise resolves per dlopen group, so
+# cross-.so typed catches and dynamic_casts match again. This replaces the
+# earlier LD_PRELOAD of libsofficeapp/libvclplug_gtk3lo/libsfxlo, which
+# only unified the types those three libraries happened to export.
 
 # linked build needs additional settings
 if [ -e "${sd_prog}/ooenv" ] ; then
-- 
2.55.0

